   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_call600_rrtm_lw_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NLAYERS = 103, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF@0e52608 (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and inside SUBROUTINE RRTM/RTRN, dump scm_ref2_600.json, tile column 0). RRTM has no standalone driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. This document runs the WHOLE longwave chain from the WRF column state: RRTMColumn (MM5ATM) -> RRTMSetcoef -> RRTMGasOptics (TAUGB1-16 + GASABS) -> RTRNSweep -> RRTMLWHeating, each stage fed by the previous one through variable_map/param_to_var edges into the stages' `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters (the mount-edge libraries lower the `input_<x>` rewrite targets to those parameters); only the column state (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, q*, cldfra, dz8w, pi3d), the surface scalars (tsk, emiss, co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr) and WRF's zero cross-section columns are prescribed. Tolerances are END-TO-END, wider than the stages' own because the sweep now consumes the gas optics' quantised ITR (exact up to +/-1 flips of the 1/5000 transition-fraction index; rrtm_gas_optics.esm) instead of the dumped ITR, and each flip perturbs one g-point optical depth: fluxes Linf abs 5e-3 W/m^2 (measured up to 3.3e-3 at call 1440, thin cirrus; 2.2e-4 with the dumped ITR) and spot checks / glw / olr rel 2e-5 (measured 1.3e-5), HTR Linf abs 5e-3 K/day and spot checks rel 1e-4 at the three largest-|HTR| layers (HTR is a real32 difference of O(300 W/m^2) fluxes over O(6 hPa)), dTdt/dthdt Linf abs 2e-8 K/s (measured 1.5e-8 at call 1440, 4e-9 at call 600; the heating stage alone is 2.4e-10 with dumped fluxes). The column-setup identities (col_tz, col_tavel, col_tbound) keep the stage tolerances. The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: call 600 (00:00 UTC, night), cirrus (cldfra = 1 in the ice layers, taucloud > 0).",
